From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:58:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Blur the Glassy bar only behind its strip

The bar surface spans its screen and is clear past the strip it paints.
With the bar-glassy layer rule, Hyprland blurs everything that changes
under the whole surface and ignore_alpha then discards it outside the
strip: a video playing in a window under the bar costs a near full-screen
blur every frame.

Name the strip as the surface's blur region (BackgroundEffect,
ext-background-effect-v1) while the bar is glassy, so the compositor can
limit the blur to it. The strip looks the same: the layer rule's
ignore_alpha still shapes the blur inside it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml b/shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml
index af39ddf271..c5bac4cd0b 100644
--- a/shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml
+++ b/shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml
@@ -1784,14 +1784,23 @@ Item {
     // the new size until the next frame lands, and the size can't come from
     // anchoring all four edges either, which would void the exclusive zone
     // (layer-shell reserves space from the one anchored edge) and drop tiled
-    // windows behind the bar. Glassy blur stays on the strip: Hyprland's
-    // ignore_alpha leaves the clear rest of the surface unblurred.
+    // windows behind the bar. Glassy blur stays on the strip: the surface
+    // names the strip as its blur region (ext-background-effect-v1), so the
+    // compositor blurs only what is behind the strip, not everything that
+    // changes anywhere under the clear rest of the surface. Hyprland's
+    // ignore_alpha (bar-glassy) still shapes the blur inside the strip.
     implicitWidth: root.vertical ? (screen ? screen.width : thickness) : 0
     implicitHeight: root.vertical ? 0 : (screen ? screen.height : thickness)
     color: "transparent"
     surfaceFormat.opaque: false
     WlrLayershell.namespace: "omarchy-bar"
     WlrLayershell.layer: WlrLayer.Top
+    BackgroundEffect.blurRegion: root.glassy && !root.transparent ? glassStripRegion : null
+
+    Region {
+      id: glassStripRegion
+      item: barStrip
+    }
 
     // Whether the active workspace on this screen holds a real fullscreen
     // window, which fades the bar out.
-- 
